      "id": 1,
      "text": "Helena was incorporated as a town in 1890, marking its formal establishment in Georgia's history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helena%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "On January 1, 2015, Helena merged with nearby McRae, creating the city of McRae‑Helena after legislative approval in 2014.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helena%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nestled in the Blue Ridge Mountains, Helena lies along the Chattahoochee River, offering scenic Appalachian vistas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://helenchamber.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The region's heritage includes Cherokee burial mounds and early 1900s gold mining and timber operations that fueled its growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://helenchamber.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "No record explains why the name 'Helena' was chosen for this community, leaving its origin a local mystery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helena%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Helena is home to the Helen Arts and Heritage Council and the Sautee Nacoochee Community Center, preserving local culture and history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
